5, hvigor, JAVA_HOME requirement to avoid the Java Runtime error), the successful build output producing the unsigned hap, the two warnings about exception handling and missing signing config, and the successful install onto the emulator with matching bundle and API version details, then starting the spec entry section.\n\nThis is a single-page app routed through main_pages.json and EntryAbility loading the Index page directly with no router/Navigation layer. I'm mapping out where the UI pieces live: the search reset arrow icon, the info bar, the symbol grid and its display component rendering characters as text, a data typo at line 491, and the search submit handler, before noting the component's state variables including one (symbolTest) that appears unused.\n\nTracking tablet-mode storage via AppStorage, the child display component's props (symbol, selected link, colors, font weight), and the capsule button component that copies text to clipboard and swaps in a placeholder emoji on first appearance only. The data model is a flat array of ~3195 symbol entries fed through a lazy-loading data source keyed by unicode, with no network or persistent storage involved—just AppStorage for screen state and a color resource file for theming, plus a Python script used to generate the data.\n\nThe glyph-name typo likely originates from the font's cmap table itself rather than the app code. I'm also noting reusable patterns worth reapplying: the capsule button for copyable text, the SymbolGlyph-plus-icon pattern for the reset control, the horizontal scroll layout, and some commented-out code hinting at the original author's intent to dynamically build SymbolGlyph resources from names.\n\nWhat's still missing is substantial though: the '^' toggle and its operation panel, the full color picker with its three groups of dots/palette/capsules/reset, the segmented rendering-strategy control, and the actual grid rendering via SymbolGlyph since Text can't support fontColor arrays or rendering strategies. There's a real technical risk around dynamic resource lookup by name since hundreds of symbol names aren't in the SDK's compile-time table, plus inconsistencies like one icon existing under a different id than expected. I also note there are no ids anywhere in the code, and that the baseline already has the spring-edge horizontal scroll behavior verified on-device, so I should treat that as something not to regress. On the environment side, everything needed is local — no login, server, or test data dependencies, and clipboard copy requires no special permissions.\n\nNow I'm thinking through observability concerns: without any `.id()` tags, tests relying on dumpLayout will miss off-screen components like the bookmark button until the user swipes, which matters for how the spec's scene 5 should be tested. Switching grid items from Text to SymbolGlyph removes their text content","startTime":1792410019188,"lastModifiedTime":1792410041800},{"id":"toolu_bdrk_01SWHjzwpVpQwjWs318QuHmz","type":"TOOL","toolName":"run_command","params":{"command":"cd /Users/bress/Documents/code/harmonycup-work/sym-combo-customize && python3 - <<'EOF'\nimport json\nd=json.load(open('logs/baseline/b0-launch.json'))\ndef walk(n):\n    a=n.get('attributes',{})\n    if a.get('type') in ('SymbolGlyph','Scroll','Button') and 'StatusBar' not in a.get('id','') and 'Component' not in a.get('id',''):\n        print(json.dumps(a,ensure_ascii=False)); \n    for c in n.get('children',[]): walk(c)\nwalk(d)\nEOF","description":"Show full dump attributes for key components","prefix_rule":"[\"python3\"]"},"toolState":"executed","result":{"output":"Command executed successfully.\nExit code: 0\nOutput:\n{\"accessibilityId\": \"7\", \"backgroundColor\": \"#00000000\", \"backgroundImage\": \"empty source\", \"blur\": \"\", \"bounds\": \"[70,2467][1238,2607]\", \"checkable\": \"false\", \"checked\": \"false\", \"clickable\": \"false\", \"clip\": \"true\", \"description\": \"\", \"displayId\": \