nsions of detail.\n\nTo keep the thirty-plus items manageable, I'm defining shared defaults (entry point, baseline data, \"not applicable\" network behavior, and return/background behavior) that each item can reference with a short justification rather than restating everything, satisfying the requirement to explain \"not applicable\" cases. I'm now listing out the scenes starting with the color picker item.\n\nItem A1 covers the clickable '^' toggle needing a selector id. A2 assumes the panel starts collapsed since the spec implies expansion. A3 is the tap that expands it, A4 is the reverse collapse (less certain), and A5 is the panel showing the three color groups — primary, secondary, and background — as visible text labels.\n\nA6 confirms each group has multiple preset color dots. A7-A9 map each group's dot tap to its respective color slot (primary → fontColor[0], secondary → fontColor[1], background → bg color), though the exact background mapping remains unconfirmed. A10 is about the grid immediately re-rendering all symbols in the newly selected colors.\n\nThe capsule button shows the system name of the currently selected color, defaulting to things like \"accent\" or \"connected,\" and tapping it likely copies that name for convenience. I'm marking the selected-dot visual state as unconfirmed since the spec is silent on it, and noting that color selection shouldn't affect the info bar, search, or current selection.\n\nFor the reset flow, there's a counterclockwise arrow icon beside the color picker that reverts primary color to accent, secondary to connected, and background to undefined/none per spec, with the grid re-rendering using defaults — presumably matching the cold-start initial values. I'm treating reset's effect on render strategy/search as unconfirmed, expecting idempotent behavior on repeated clicks, and separately noting the search bar has its own reset icon row to consider.\n\nMoving to Scene 3's strategy panel, there's a three-segment SegmentButton labeled SINGLE/MULTIPLE_COLOR/MULTIPLE_OPACITY (language unconfirmed), defaulting to SINGLE selection. Clicking a segment switches the active strategy and re-renders all grid symbols accordingly, with a capsule showing the current strategy name that's reasonably assumed to be copyable.\n\nIn practice, MULTIPLE_COLOR applies multiple font colors, SINGLE uses only the primary color, and MULTIPLE_OPACITY varies opacity of the primary color -- with the final state after rapid toggling just reflecting the last selection.\n\nScene 4 introduces a renamed icon (bookmark_on_bookmark, id 476, U+0F01E2) where searching the full name or substrings like \"kmark_on_bookmark\" should still match it, and selecting the result shows the name capsule with its id and code point.\n\n","startTime":1792410227155,"lastModifiedTime":1792410249759},{"id":"toolu_bdrk_01A73NXVjN6rFdyGyyLZn5Kd","type":"TOOL","toolName":"write_file","params":{"content":{"$blob":"sha256:bb7c22a83aaebc62ecf8feba5445d4d2b69f28083a002edb4a36bb2e4e203fe6","version":1,"encoding":"utf8","byteLength":3352,"compression":"none"},"file_path":"/Users/bress/Documents/code/harmonycup-work/sym-combo-customize/spec/acceptance.md"},"toolState":"executed","result":{"output":"Write file success","metadata":{"relativePath":"spec/acceptance.md","absolutePath":"/Users/bress/Documents/code/harmonycup-work/sym-combo-customize/spec/acceptance.md","diff":{"add":45,"remove":0},"resolution":"absolute","originalContent":null,"content":{"$blob":"sha256:bb7c22a83aaebc62ecf8feba5445d4d2b69f28083a002edb4a36bb2e4e203fe6","version":1,"encoding":"utf8","byteLength":3352,"compression":"none"},"askReview":false,"runMode":"yolo"}},"accepted":true,"isRebuilt":false}]},{"id":"6ad602cc3e412730c6a90884","discard":false,"metrics":{"duration":24216},"hasUnpairedToolUse":false,"children":[{"id":"toolu_bdrk_01AGb22etEUcLtGohR7mBBzi","type":"TOOL","toolName":"edit_file","params":{"file_path":"/Users/bress/Documents/code/harmonycup-work/sym-combo-customi